# Laundry App Vocabulary

This document defines the terminology and vocabulary used throughout the Laundry App codebase to ensure consistent and precise communication when interacting with the AI assistant.

## Project Structure

### Top-Level Directories

- **`backend/`**: Node.js/Express REST API backend
- **`admin-panel/`**: React-based web application for mart administration
- **`customer-app/`**: Flutter mobile application for customers
- **`delivery-app/`**: Flutter mobile application for delivery partners
- **`shared/`**: Shared utilities, types, and configurations across applications
- **`docs/`**: Project documentation, API specs, and architecture diagrams
- **`.tmp/`**: Temporary files and experimental code (excluded from version control)
- **`.cursor/`**: AI assistant configuration and context storage
- **`docker/`**: Docker configuration and compose files
- **`scripts/`**: Build, deployment, and utility scripts

## Backend Terminology

### Backend Structure (`backend/`)

- **`src/`**: Source code directory
  - **`controllers/`**: HTTP request handlers and route definitions
  - **`services/`**: Business logic and orchestration layer
  - **`middleware/`**: Express middleware (auth, validation, error handling, logging)
  - **`utils/`**: Helper functions and utilities
  - **`config/`**: Configuration files and environment setup
  - **`types/`**: TypeScript type definitions and interfaces
  - **`constants/`**: Application constants and enums
- **`prisma/`**: Database schema and migrations
  - **`schema.prisma`**: Prisma schema definition
  - **`migrations/`**: Database migration files
  - **`seed.ts`**: Database seeding script
- **`tests/`**: Test files (unit and integration tests)
- **`uploads/`**: Temporary upload directory (excluded from git)
- **`logs/`**: Application logs (excluded from git)
- **`Dockerfile`**: Docker container configuration
- **`package.json`**: Node.js dependencies and scripts
- **`.env.example`**: Environment variable template

### Backend Components

- **Controller**: Handles HTTP requests, validates input, calls services, formats responses
- **Service**: Contains business logic, orchestrates operations, manages transactions
- **Middleware**: Intercepts requests for authentication, validation, logging, error handling
- **Util**: Helper functions for common operations (distance calculation, file upload, etc.)
- **DTO**: Data Transfer Object for request/response validation
- **Model**: Prisma-generated database model types
- **Route**: Express route definition mapping URLs to controllers
- **Repository Pattern**: Direct usage of Prisma Client for database operations

## Frontend Terminology

### Admin Panel (`admin-panel/`)

React-based web application with the following structure:

- **`src/`**: Source code directory
  - **`components/`**: Reusable React components
    - **`common/`**: Common UI components (buttons, inputs, cards, etc.)
    - **`layout/`**: Layout components (header, sidebar, footer)
    - **`features/`**: Feature-specific components
  - **`pages/`**: Page components mapped to routes
    - **`Dashboard/`**: Analytics and metrics dashboard
    - **`Orders/`**: Order management pages
    - **`Customers/`**: Customer management pages
    - **`Delivery/`**: Delivery staff management pages
    - **`Services/`**: Service catalog management
    - **`Reports/`**: Reporting and analytics pages
  - **`hooks/`**: Custom React hooks
  - **`services/`**: API client services
  - **`store/`**: State management (Context API or Redux)
  - **`utils/`**: Utility functions
  - **`types/`**: TypeScript type definitions
  - **`constants/`**: Application constants
  - **`assets/`**: Static assets (images, fonts, etc.)
  - **`styles/`**: Global styles and themes

